AB  - The government and business have been closely watching healthcare industry improvements related to the IoT because of the potential they hold to improve patient diagnosis and research. Privacy and security are major issues with healthcare data due to its sensitive nature, especially when user data needs to be sent to data centres for data mining. A privacy-aware healthcare architecture based on federated learning is proposed in this paper to address these difficulties. It allows various entities to work together to train a global Privacy Aware Healthcare model without disclosing personal information. An innovative deep learning architecture called Enhanced Ghost BiNet, which combines GhostNet with the BiGRU is used by the framework to safely train local models. The model is fine-tuned using the CAh algorithm after data is cleaned and features are extracted using cuckoos. The suggested FL-CAh-HE technique is highly effective, as shown experimentally by its 99.05% detection precision. In essence, our research shows that in privacy-aware healthcare settings, federated learning, deep learning, and advanced optimisation methods may work together to improve detection accuracy, safeguard patient privacy, and guarantee secure information exchange. © 2026 IEEE.
