AB  - Wearable health devices are a breakthrough consumer electronic that enable long-term collection of physiological data and enable early warning of abnormalities in health. Nevertheless, the existing AI-based applications portray significant weakness in privacy safeguarding, interpretability, and instantaneous performance, which are further exacerbated when it comes to sensitive health information. The present work proposes a privacy-preserving, consumer wearable-specific neuro-symbolic AI model designed to mitigate these deficiencies through the integration of federated learning with symbolic reasoning. The framework also inserts a privacy saving layer of computation relying on the latest homomorphic encryption methods customized to resource-limited wearables. The methodology thus involves building hybrid neural-symbolic models that can work with data coming out of multi-modal sensors in a real-time fashion, that is, electrocardiogram (ECG) photoplethysmography (PPG), accelerometer and temperature sensors and provide clear explanations of the health assessment made. The deployment will be done through the usage of Logical Neural Networks, which will fuse external medical knowledge with the patterns achieved in the physiological data, thus, providing a foundation not only of the reliable health monitoring but also a suggestion incorporation. The empirical analysis has shown that the system is more effective than the current methods in detecting anomalies, accuracy translating to 94.8%, and that it covers privacy levels 70% less than cloud-based systems, and within a range that is latency of encryption values 35 ms, which is an optimum parameter to be used in real-time health-based monitoring. © 1975-2011 IEEE.
