TI  - NeuroShield-Diabetes: A Hybrid Nature-Inspired Neural Cryptography and Machine Learning framework for Privacy-Preserving Diabetes Data Sharing in Consumer Health
PY  - 2026
T2  - IEEE Transactions on Consumer Electronics
DO  - 10.1109/TCE.2026.3702497
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041948151?origin=resultslist
AB  - Consumer health applications for diabetes management create critical privacy vulnerabilities when sharing sensitive patient data across healthcare ecosystems, demanding lightweight cryptographic solutions for resource-constrained mobile environments. This paper presents NeuroShield-Diabetes, a hybrid framework integrating neural cryptography with machine learning for privacy-preserving diabetes data sharing on smartphones and wearables. The framework employs tree parity machines for neural key exchange, achieving cryptographic strength comparable to 2048-bit RSA with 91% reduced computational complexity measured as CPU cycles per key generation operation. Adaptive differential privacy with calibrated noise injection maintains formal guarantees (ε ≤ 0.8 for high-risk queries) while preserving 94.7% data utility for glycemic prediction. Evaluation across 5,600 diabetes patients using MIMIC-III and UCI Diabetes datasets demonstrates 73% reduction in data sharing latency versus conventional cryptographic solutions. The neural intrusion detection system achieves 92.6% accuracy in identifying malicious access attempts with sub-120ms overhead. Field deployment confirms HIPAA compliance and GDPR conformance while maintaining interoperability with existing healthcare infrastructures, establishing NeuroShield-Diabetes as a practical privacy-preserving solution for consumer diabetes applications. © 1975-2011 IEEE.
