AB  - Recent advancements in multimodal learning are revolutionizing high-stakes domains like healthcare by integrating medical imaging, genomics, and clinical text for holistic analysis. A key trend is the convergence with federated learning (FL) and privacy preservation, enabling model training on distributed sensitive data without centralization. Frameworks such as Federated Multimodal Transformers (FMT) and DermaGPT dynamically fuse modalities while maintaining data locality. To strengthen security, these systems integrate homomorphic encryption (HE) and differential privacy (DP) against inference attacks. Simultaneously, explainable AI (XAI) tools like SHAP and GradCAM are being embedded to ensure clinical transparency. Emerging frontiers include multimodal large language models (MLLMs) for report generation and quantum-entangled DP for future threats [6]. Despite progress, challenges like modality imbalance and regulatory hurdles persist. Collectively, these trends point toward distributed, interpretable, and robust systems that unlock sensitive data's potential while upholding the highest privacy and trust standards. © 2026 IEEE.
