AB  - This study presents NeuroNimbus (NN), a federated and cloud-orchestrated deep learning framework for privacy-preserving, real-time clinical decision support. NN kept data local at hospitals and used a lightweight cloud service to coordinate model updates with privacy guarantees. On MIMIC-III and eICU, NN sustained edge inference latency at 84 ms, cut aggregation rounds by 34% and cumulative transmitted bytes by 38% versus fixed scheduling, and achieved near-centralized AUC for mortality and sepsis prediction. In simulation, NN scaled to 50 heterogeneous clients without network congestion. An RL-driven scheduler (FCPO) adaptively selected clients and synchronization intervals under a byte budget while enforcing latency targets. These results indicate that NN can deliver low-latency clinical intelligence with formal privacy protections across distributed healthcare networks. © 2013 IEEE.
