UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105045463569?origin=resultslist
AB  - The centralisation of sensitive patient data and the associated privacy and regulation issues are making rapid progress in medical imaging and Machine Learning for brain tumor detection complex. Federated Learning (FL) allows group of medical organizations to learn a global model without having to share the raw data. This research proposal is based on the application of privacy-oriented federated learning with brain tumor predictions through a framework. The proposed system incorporates secure aggregation, differential privacy and homomorphic encryption with a deep convolutional neural network for classifying a heterogeneous MRI dataset for tumour detection. In our experiments, the centralized models' accuracy of of the FL model is similar. Moreover, the model meets privacy regulations and laws including GDPR and HIPAA. The framework's communication protocol reduces bandwidth utilization by 38 % and increases convergence time by 22 %. According to the results, the privacy-preserving FL can scale securely and accurately in medical AI. © 2026 IEEE.
