TI  - Enhanced brain tumor detection through spectral domain reconstruction graph neural network with privacy-preserving secure smart healthcare framework
PY  - 2026
T2  - Biomedical Signal Processing and Control
VL  - 127
C7  - 110982
DO  - 10.1016/j.bspc.2026.110982
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047680166?origin=resultslist
AB  - Medical image processing has made extensive use of spurred the creation of numerous applications and significantly expanded the therapeutic and diagnostic choices available for a variety of medical imaging issues. In this paper, an Enhanced Brain Tumor Detection through Spectral Domain Reconstruction Graph Neural Network with Privacy-Preserving Secure Smart Healthcare Framework (BTD-SDRGNN-SSH) is proposed. Here, the input images are gathered from Brain Tumor Detection 2020 dataset. The gathered images are pre-processing using Bayesian Boundary Trend Filtering (BBTF) for image normalization and cleaning. Then the pre-processed images are fed into the Refined Linear Chirplet Transform (RLCT) to extract statistical features such as Skewness, Standard Deviation, Kurtosis Features. The extracted statistical features are given into SDRGNN to detect and classify brain image as tumor and No tumor. To enhance the Triangulation Topology Aggregation Optimizer (TTAO) optimize the weight parameters of SDRGNN. The images are given to Martino Homomorphic encryption Algorithm (MHEA), which used to secure the images. The proposed BTD-SDRGNN-SSH technique is examined by the following performance metrics: accuracy, specificity, precision, recall, ROC, FI-score, computational time, error rate, detection rate. The performance of the BTD-SDRGNN-SSH method achieves 7.54%, 8.27%, 7.37% high accuracy; 7.96%, 8.79% and 6.68% higher precision and 7.85%, 6.49% and 7.48% higher recall compared with existing method respectively. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd
