TI  - Secure Cloud-based EHR Analytics using a Hybrid Homomorphic Encryption and Differential Privacy Pipeline
PY  - 2026
T2  - 7th International Conference on Electronics and Sustainable Communication Systems, ICESC 2026 - Proceedings
SP  - 103
EP  - 110
DO  - 10.1109/ICESC70182.2026.11687257
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105052171434?origin=resultslist
AB  - The problem of providing confidentiality for Electronic Health Records (EHRs) hosted in the cloud is twofold because it requires the protection of data confidentiality during computations and against output privacy attacks. Although Homomorphic Encryption (HE) protects confidential data from being leaked during computation processes, its decrypted output is vulnerable to various types of inference attacks. In turn, Differential Privacy (DP) protects sensitive information from being revealed through computation outputs while leaving computational processes unprotected. We propose a novel HE+DP hybrid pipeline in which a Cheon-Kim-Kim-Song (CKKS) scheme is utilized to perform computations securely in the encrypted domain, followed by the application of DP through the introduction of Laplacian noise to the computation results. We provide a detailed system and threat model, along with an overview of the algorithms and architecture of the designed pipeline to ensure replicability. An experimental evaluation of the proposed approach is conducted on synthetic and publicly available EHR datasets using various settings (ϵ ≥ 1.0). We show that our approach preserves near-plaintext accuracy (RMSE < 5%) with an overhead of roughly 12× compared to plaintext operations for medium-sized datasets. © 2026 IEEE.
