TI  - Federated Learning and Privacy-Preserving Techniques: A Comprehensive Review of Advancements and Challenges
PY  - 2025
T2  - International Conference on Emerging Technologies in Electronics and Green Energy, ICETEG 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ICETEG66194.2025.11472906
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105037574520?origin=resultslist
AB  - Federated Learning (FL) learning models and Privacy Protection Techniques (PPT) are important in machine learning. They meet the urgent need for distributed learning while maintaining data security and privacy. This overview article provides an in-depth overview of the latest developments and problems of FL and PPT, and provides a thorough understanding of their importance in various areas such as the Internet of Things (IoT) applications, healthcare and finance. Starting with homomorphic encryption, secure multi-party computing, trusted execution environments, and differential privacy, the study goes on to explain the basic ideas of FL and several PPT approaches. The discussion then dives into the latest developments in FL designs, optimization algorithms, and safe model aggregation strategies, emphasizing the progress made in improving communication effectiveness and protecting data privacy during model updates. This paper goes into great length about the challenges FL faces, despite its potential. Device heterogeneity, communication obstacles, and possible security vulnerabilities are some of these difficulties. The article also proposes future research topics, such the integration of FL with edge computing, blockchain, and secure multi-party computing, to close existing gaps and improve the field. To highlight the importance of FL and PPT to enable secure and comprehensive machine learning applications, this article concludes by highlighting the need for concerted efforts to overcome remaining obstacles and realize the full potential of learning models decentralized and maintain confidentiality. © 2025 IEEE.
