AB  - Industrial fault diagnosis in distributed manufacturing faces twin bottlenecks: data scarcity and privacy constraints. While existing federated generative models attempt to bridge these gaps, they often overlook data heterogeneity (varying fault distributions), leading to sub-optimal convergence and low-fidelity synthetic data generation. This paper presents FL-GAN, an adaptive heterogeneity-aware framework specifically engineered for privacy-preserving industrial diagnostics. Our contributions are threefold: (1) a Hierarchical Federated Architecture that decouples global feature alignment from local adaptation; (2) an Adaptive Weight Aggregation (AWA) strategy based on Data Quality (DQS) and Distribution Similarity (DSS); and (3) a Hybrid Privacy Mechanism combining LDP and lightweight homomorphic encryption. Experimental results on three real-world datasets show that FL-GAN reduces FID scores by 27.3% and enhances diagnostic accuracy by 16.8% compared to FedGAN. Notably, the framework maintains a Membership Inference Attack (MIA) success rate close to 50% (random guess baseline), ensuring robust protection for sensitive industrial data. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
