TI  - Research on privacy-preserving logistic regression scheme based on homomorphic encryption
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings of SPIE - The International Society for Optical Engineering
VL  - 13644
C7  - 136441T
DO  - 10.1117/12.3070276
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105009403006?origin=resultslist
AB  - Along with the rapid development of cloud computing and machine learning technology, a large number of sensitive data are uploaded to the cloud server for processing and analysis, which leads to serious privacy-related issues. Against this background, this paper proposes a privacy-preserving logistic regression scheme based on homomorphic encryption, which mainly utilizes the Cheon-Kim-Kim-Song (CKKS) floating-point vector homomorphic encryption algorithm to ensure the security of users’ sensitive data. More specifically, the proposed scheme decomposes the machine learning algorithm into a series of basic operation modules, such as addition, multiplication, inner product, rotation, and function, thereby adopting a multi-party interactive method to address complex operations that cannot be directly implemented within the ciphertext domain. Relevant experimental results indicate that the proposed scheme is capable of maintaining a high classification accuracy while protecting data privacy, with the accuracy rate reaching 90.76% and 83.94% on the open source breast cancer dataset and Pima Indians diabetes dataset respectively. Moreover, further analysis demonstrates that the proposed scheme has an excellent performance in computing efficiency and security, which furnishes a practical solution for machine learning related to privacy preservation in a cloud environment. © 2025 SPIE.
