AB  - Advanced cryptography integrates with federated learning in healthcare for privacy-preserving machine learning. The research aims to enable collaborative training across institutions for breast cancer classification, emphasizing data security with a secure federated learning architecture and homomorphic encryption. Raw data is kept decentralized and encrypted to protect sensitive medical information. The system uses federated learning and the OpenFHE library to securely aggregate model updates, allowing authorized hospitals to access the global model. Experiments with the BreakHis dataset show good performance, confirming the framework's effectiveness in balancing model performance and data security. This study demonstrates the potential of federated learning and homomorphic encryption in healthcare privacy and security, offering a scalable solution. Future work will explore broader datasets and real-world applications. © Grenze Scientific Society, 2025.
