AB  - Aiming at the limited accuracy of single modality analysis methods and the need for data privacy protection in the early diagnosis of pulmonary nodules, this study designed an intelligent segmentation and benign and malignant analysis system that integrates multimodal images and clinical data. Methodologically, a segmentation model based on an improved 3D U-Net is proposed, which combines homomorphic encryption and a federated learning framework to complete data processing and model collaborative training in a distributed environment. Experiments were carried out using the LIDC-IDRI dataset, and the system outperformed traditional methods in key indicators such as Dice coefficient, IoU, and AUC. Ablation experiments further verified the important role of multimodal fusion and enhancement modules in performance improvement. The research results show that the proposed system not only has good segmentation and classification performance, but also can effectively protect patient data privacy, providing a feasible reference for intelligent screening of pulmonary nodules and clinical decision-making assistance. © 2025 IEEE.
