AB  - Multi-Key Homomorphic Encryption (MKHE) has been applied across diverse scenarios, including convolutional neural networks, federated learning, finance and healthcare, yet its efficiency remains less than satisfactory. Notably, the relinearization process, particularly its non-linear operations, has become a critical performance bottleneck. At present, existing MKHE schemes all apply a fixed decomposition function across all levels. In this paper, we present a level-aware multi-key relinearization method customized for the improved CDKS MKHE scheme (ACNS 2024). Moreover, we rigorously prove its correctness and analyze noise variations. Theoretical analysis shows that, compared with the improved CDKS relinearization algorithm using a fixed digit length r=1 , our proposed method reduces the number of Number Theoretic Transform (NTT) operations by 38.90%, 42.56%, and 45.23% respectively when the number of participants k is 2, 4, and 8. © 2013 IEEE.
