UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105040184675?origin=resultslist
AB  - The Internet of Medical Things consumer electronics (IoMT-CE) devices integrated with deep learning (DL) model have achieved remarkable success in the medical field, which provides intelligent diagnostic assistance. However, as DL technologies evolve rapidly, a key challenge lies in how to continuously enhance the intelligent assisted diagnostic capabilities of IoMT-CE devices. Federated learning (FL), an effective distributed learning framework, holds great potential to address this issue. In this article, we propose a novel secure and efficient FL scheme for IoMT-CE devices based on consortium blockchain. In this scheme, all participating hospitals, the aggregation server (AS), and the noise parameter server (NPS) establish a consortium blockchain, where hash values and signature data are stored. Paillier homomorphic encryption (HE) and noise mechanisms are employed to protect patient privacy, while an elliptic curve cryptography-based proxy re-encryption (ECC-PRE) strategy is adopted to ensure model security between the AS and IoMT-CE devices. Furthermore, this scheme guarantees that model updates are applied correctly, even when local models cannot be uploaded to hospitals. Finally, the performance of our proposed scheme is verified. The results demonstrate that the encryption mechanisms have almost no impact on model accuracy, and the proposed scheme proves to be robust and fault-tolerant in cases of disconnection. © 1975-2011 IEEE.
