AB  - heart diseases are one of the leading causes of morbidity and mortality worldwide. The danger the disease induces and set of complexity and dependency on various factors thereby it requires some advanced approach for early detection and prediction. This literature review provides an in-depth analysis of the various machine learning techniques that can be used for heart rate prediction and prevention. The article focuses on training the model based on both clinical and non-clinical parameters as the machine learning models built and trained using these parameters can offer personalized health recommendations and risk assessments. By integrating the clinical parameters, machine learning algorithms can significantly improve the accuracy of prediction and thereby help in early intervention strategies. The article focuses on usage of Deep Neural Network more specifically the usage of CNN in the prediction of heart diseases based on data collected rather than the most widely used random forest algorithm in predicting cardio-vascular diseases due to higher accuracy and also real time monitoring and processing capabilities. The integration of CNNs in IoT devices for continuous monitoring and data processing is also discussed in the article, thereby highlighting the potential of using CNN in personalized health recommendations and also in early intervention and treatment strategies.  © 2025 IEEE.
