DO  - 10.1109/ICCDS64403.2025.11209601
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105023832531?origin=resultslist
AB  - In the medical context, proper and secure document handling is paramount to protect sensitive patient data while ensuring accessibility and integrity. This paper presents an OCR-capable secure data storage facility for an Intelligent Document Management System (IDMS) that utilizes Blockchain for immutable storage, Homomorphic Encryption for protecting confidentiality, and Federated Learning for intelligent access control. Optical Character Recognition (OCR) is used to scan and recover text from medical histories, prescriptions, and free-text notes, making it easy to integrate with the database. Blockchain technology provides safe storage of documents through the use of a decentralized ledger that prevents any unauthorized modifications. To enhance security, Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) and Interplanetary File System (IPFS) are paired for secure document storage and retrieval, ensuring scalability and reduced overhead. Also, OCR deep learning models such as Tesseract 5.0 with added Transformer capabilities are employed to improve text recognition accuracy. The proposed system enhances the protection, integrity, and compatibility of the data while providing smooth document access across healthcare networks. Experimental results demonstrate a 95% accuracy in text extraction using OCR and a 30% reduction in retrieval latency compared to traditional document management systems. This approach provides a robust, Al-driven, blockchain-based document management system for modern-day healthcare environments. © 2025 IEEE.
