TI  - AgriSmartNet: A quantum-inspired secure framework for smart sensing, clustering, and PPO-SADS decision-making in precision agriculture
PY  - 2026
T2  - Sustainable Computing: Informatics and Systems
VL  - 50
C7  - 101340
DO  - 10.1016/j.suscom.2026.101340
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105034149828?origin=resultslist
AB  - Modern precision agriculture requires adaptive, data-driven strategies to optimize resource use, enhance productivity, and ensure environmental sustainability. Traditional farming methods often struggle to respond to dynamic environmental conditions, resulting in inefficient irrigation, suboptimal fertilization, inadequate pest control, and insecure farm data handling. To address these challenges, we propose AgriSmartNet, a comprehensive framework integrating intelligent sensing, adaptive clustering, AI-driven decision-making, secure communication, and decentralized blockchain-based storage for real-time precision agriculture. The Event-Driven Sensing Protocol (EDSP) activates sensors only upon significant environmental changes, reducing energy consumption and redundant measurements. The Adaptive Spatial-Temporal Convergence Algorithm (ASTCA), combined with quantum-inspired reinforcement learning, enables energy-efficient clustering, prioritizes high-value data transmission, and minimizes communication overhead. AgriFortNet, leveraging graph reinforcement learning and quantum-secure homomorphic encryption, ensures secure, energy-aware routing while preserving data confidentiality. Adaptive decisions are made through a PPO-based Secure Adaptive Decision System (PPO-SADS), optimizing irrigation, pest control, and soil health interventions in real time. AgriChain Blockchain provides immutable, decentralized storage, supporting tamper-proof farm records, smart contract execution, and reputation-based trust management. Extensive experiments on simulated and real-world farms show that AgriSmartNet improves resource efficiency by 35%, reduces energy consumption by 40%, achieves 98% crop health classification accuracy, supports 250 secure transactions per second, and lowers data transmission latency by 55% compared to existing approaches. By balancing computational efficiency, network reliability, data security, and autonomous decision-making, AgriSmartNet transforms conventional farming into a self-optimizing, resilient, and sustainable ecosystem, offering actionable insights for deploying intelligent agriculture systems across diverse environments. © 2026
