AB  - This paper proposes an Intelligent Attendance Management System proposed to improve classroom monitoring with AI-based facial recognition, engagement analysis, and privacy-preserving encryption. To avoid spoofing attendance without actual presence like printed pictures, video replays, and 3D mask attacks, the system includes anti-spoofing facial recognition based on Deep Neural Networks (DNNs) with FaceNet texture and blink-based liveness detection. ResNet-powered real-time emotion detection monitors the levels of attention among students, providing useful information on participation and effectiveness of learning. The mask detection module, deployed via YOLOv8 (a CNN method), provides accurate identification even when faces are partially masked, to facilitate health safety measures. The test accuracy of 94.0% by the proposed system represents a significant improvement from the baseline accuracy of 78.68%. Detection of forgeries and detection of duplicate attendance also increase transparency and accountability. For the sake of data security, Fully Homomorphic Encryption (FHE) based on the CKKS (Cheon-Kim-Kim-Song) scheme supports encrypted face comparison without revealing sensitive biometric information. Experimental outcomes under diverse conditions prove the reliability, effectiveness, and robust privacy protection of the system. © 2025 IEEE.
