AB  - In recent years, advancements in Artificial Intelligence (AI) have significantly improved communication systems in terms of data transmission rate, latency, and accuracy, along with high demand to support a variety of new applications and services, including Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR), Metaverse, large-scale Internet of Things (IoT), e-health, autonomous and flying vehicles. AI is pivotal in developing next-generation communication systems, such as 5G and beyond, and is expected to play an even more significant role in the future. However, using AI methods brings significant challenges due to centralized high computing demand, data diversity, and security concerns. Fortunately, Federated Learning (FL) is a decentralized form of machine learning that offers a promising solution to these challenges. This paper proposes a cryptographic FL-based channel estimation model using AI models for next-generation networks to encrypt the data to prevent privacy attacks. The study uses homomorphic encryption (HE) to address this issue, providing a secure multi-party computation protocol (SMCP) to safeguard AI-based channel estimation models.  © 2023 IEEE.
