TI  - AI-Augmented Cybersecurity Architectures for Privacy-Preserving Data Pipelines in Dynamic Smart Environments
PY  - 2025
T2  - IEEE International Conference on Innovate for Humanitarian: Tech Solutions for Global Challenge, ICIH 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ICIH67754.2025.11608625
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105046380794?origin=resultslist
AB  - A secure and privacy preserving data flow within distributed and dynamic large scale environments has become an essential issue in the age of hyper connected smart environments. In this study, a new Dual Layer AI Augmented Federated Confidentiality Model DL AIFCM that can protect data pipelines and still be highly efficient and protect the privacy of users is presented. The suggested architecture combines federated learning with homomorphic encryption and differential privacy to make sure that sensitive data does not leave its local setting in the process of distributed training and, therefore, does not necessitate the need of exchanging raw data. The proposed DL AIFCM framework has been evaluated in a simulated smart city environment with multiple IoT devices, demonstrating its capability to detect cyber threats in real-time while preserving user privacy, making it suitable for practical deployment in urban infrastructure, healthcare, and intelligent transportation systems. Adaptive Threat Intelligence Layer ATIL is a reinforcement learning that operates independently to identify anomalies, judge trust, and react real-time throughout the system. Moreover, such verification protocol can be based on Zero Knowledge Proofs and guarantee integrity of data without flash over to confidentiality. In order to mitigate the complexity and topology volatility of smart environments, a Graph Neural Network GNN module performs on-demand mapping of changes in the network and flaws. It also enhances the architecture with Self- Healing Response Engine SHRE that allows automatic mitigation by mode of policy reconfiguration and isolating routes. The composite nature of these constructed elements creates a high quality AI enhanced cybersecurity system against rapidly changing cyber threats without data privacy compromises, which is highly applicable in the actual application of smart infrastructures. The suggested DL AIFCM technique attains an overall accuracy of 96.1 percent in identifying and alleviating cybersecurity risks in dynamic smart settings. © 2025 IEEE.
