AB  - Data breach and data theft has become a repulsive problem in the digital world and medical data is the most vulnerable in this case as it contains numerous information of patients which can hinder a patient's personal life. Moreover, due to patients' rights and confidentiality, hospital's are unwilling to share the medical data to third parties. Also, Brain tumour is one of the most occurring disease as everyday, around the globe vast amount of MRI image are taken. Many existing models have been introduced throughout the decades to detect brain tumors, mostly based on Neural Network models. To secure the MRI images and protect patient rights, we have worked on a technique based on Partial Homomorphic Encryption (PHE) which produces encrypted images while keeping most of the features intact. As a result, existing NN models can produce a higher accuracy by extracting features from the encrypted images and also reduces the time complexity of established Paillier cryptosystem. We were able to achieve max 82% accuracy using a VGG-19 model. Using our proposed model we can safely and securely read encrypted medical image data via our PHE method while being efficient enough to be used on a mass scale in the medical industry. © 2023 IEEE.
