AB  - Fully homomophic encryption enables private computation over sensitive data, such as medical data, via potentially quantum-safe primitives. In this extended abstract we provide an overview of an implementation of a private-key fully homomorphic encryption scheme in a protocol for private Naive Bayes classification. This protocol allows a data owner to privately classify her data point without direct access to the learned model. We implement this protocol by performing privacy-preserving classification of breast cancer data as benign or malignant. © 2018, Springer International Publishing AG, part of Springer Nature.
