AB  - Data security is becoming more important as the number of people using Cloud-based services and programs grows. Data stored in the cloud may be protected in a variety of ways, with even more techniques under active investigation. In this article, we outline how we have used encryption and categorisation to keep sensitive information safe. To avoid security risks, we employ the K-NN classification algorithm to sort the data into categories based on their requirements, and then encrypt the categories that include sensitive information. We put the framework through its paces using the Java emulator. The framework has several purposes, but one of them is to facilitate high-performance computing through cloud services. Infrastructure-as-a-service, to provide a service is the primary application. However, we think the suggested architecture will be useful in three downstream use cases: genomics, exploration for oil and gas, and ray tracing. © 2024, Scibulcom Ltd.. All rights reserved.
