AB  - At present, the incidence of cancer continues to rise and has become one of the most common causes of death. In order to improve the survival rate of cancer patients, machine learning and deep learning have been applied to the medical diagnosis process. However, in recent years, data leakage incidents have occurred frequently, some tumor images in medical diagnosis have been published on the Internet without the consent of patients. In order to protect the privacy of patients and improve the security of medical diagnosis, we introduce homomorphic encryption algorithm. In this paper, based on the nnUNet segmentation algorithm, we combine the fully homomorphic encryption method to propose the HEnnUNet scheme. In this scheme, some common data enhancement methods are utilized to process the training set images. Meanwhile, in order to increase the rate of extracting features of the prediction model in the encrypted domain, we design the computation method of the prediction model in the encrypted domain utilizing the characteristics of ciphertext. The convolution method of image data in the encrypted domain is improved, the structure of convolutional and sampling layers of image data in the encrypted domain is optimized. This paper applies BraTS2018 and BraTS2019 datasets to verify the effectiveness of our proposed method. The research we have performed suggests that our proposed method can effectively protect privacy data and prevent malicious attacks. Facts have proved that our segmentation performance is satisfying and can be applied as a reference for diagnosis and treatment.  © 2023 ACM.
