TI  - Development of AI Models Driven by Blockchain for Privacy-Preserving Data Exchange in Personal Data Management and Healthcare Systems
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Advanced Computing Technologies, ICACT 2025
SP  - 260
EP  - 266
DO  - 10.1109/ICACT67549.2025.11351450
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105033646453?origin=resultslist
AB  - As reliance on AI in personal data management and health care systems increases, concerns about data privacy and security grow. Conventional AI models improve their predictions and performance by access to sensitive personal information, placing users at the risk of privacy concerns and data breaches. Blockchain is a decentralized, secure, and transparent framework for managing data - one that holds potential for answering these privacy challenges. This work looks into forming up AI models based on blockchain technology to support privacy-preserving data interchange in personal data management and healthcare systems. We aim to develop a system that embeds privacy in data sharing - to do so, we will leverage the benefits of blockchain, such as encryption, immutability and no central controller, augmented with advanced AI techniques. They proposed a framework based on smart contracts that can automatically grant data access and verify if the AI model was working on the encrypted data without showing personal or sensitive information. To address this challenge, federated learning and homomorphic encryption techniques are introduced to facilitate the training of distributed AI models while ensuring data privacy in decentralized networks. Finally, the research investigates blockchainpowered AI models in healthcare systems, which necessitate data privacy due to stringent regulatory frameworks, to assess their performance, scalability, and security. This research helps pave the way for more responsible, transparent and impactful AI-driven solutions for personal data management and healthcare systems by illustrating the synergistic capabilities of AI and blockchain supporting secure and privacy-respecting data exchange. The findings indicate that by leveraging the power of blockchain, it is possible to bolster the confidence and trustworthiness of Artificial Intelligence systems, without breaching data protection regulations while not impacting the advantages of AI innovation in crucial sectors.  © 2025 IEEE.
